{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Cause established: reading (a), runner contention -- NOT a leaked process/handle.\n\nDecisive evidence from run 33846424069, job 100939218689:\n\n* the failure is subprocess.TimeoutExpired on `git rev-parse HEAD` after 5s, with\n  `<Popen: returncode: -9 ...>` -- the child was ALIVE and killed by the timeout, so it\n  was running, not wedged on a git resource.\n* the same run emitted 400 [rebar-ci-timing] warnings (threshold 1.0s), topping out at\n  `built_distributions fixture_setup elapsed=4.562s` on a DIFFERENT worker (gw1). Ordinary\n  fixture setup on that runner reaches 91% of the probe's fixed 5s bound.\n\nReading (b) has no mechanism, and the ticket's premise for it is factually wrong:\n\n* the blamed test drives a shell STUB npm (_SUCCEEDS: `mkdir -p node_modules; exit 0`)\n  under tmp_path. It does NOT provision a real Node toolchain -- it is one of the cheapest\n  tests in the file. There is no real npm ci/esbuild child to leak.\n* `git rev-parse HEAD` reads .git/HEAD plus refs and takes NO lock, so no leaked handle can\n  serialize against it.\n* patched-clock ruled out: CPython binds `from time import monotonic as _time` in\n  subprocess, so the timeout check is immune to a time.monotonic patch.\n* leaked PATH ruled out experimentally: monkeypatch (function-scoped, non-autouse) is\n  finalized BEFORE the autouse guard's post-yield, so the probe runs with the session PATH.\n\nSo the defect is the BOUND, not the test. Fix: _run_git_probe re-samples a timed-out\nattempt up to GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS (3); the final attempt sits outside the retry loop so a\nPERSISTENT timeout still raises loudly. No sleep between attempts (the elapsed per-attempt\ntimeout is the backoff, and sleeping would re-introduce the patched-time.sleep hazard\n_stable_subprocess_time defends against).\n\nGuard not weakened, and it is enforced: mutating head/porcelain to swallow TimeoutExpired\nfails 3 tests. A real HEAD move is still detected. The e2e test is untouched.\n\nGerrit change 2618: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2618\nVerification dispatch: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/33855430270"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788511918166679001,"uuid":"668c906c-6237-40bb-87cb-8caf42bf546e"}